## B. Candidate Priorities  

### B1. Initial 15 candidate priorities (UK‑wide relevance)  
1. Remote monitoring for COPD/asthma to prevent winter exacerbations  
2. AI‑assisted triage and clinical decision support in urgent care  
3. Community point‑of‑care (POC) diagnostics for respiratory infections  
4. Virtual wards for acute respiratory illness and heart failure  
5. Targeted vaccination (flu, COVID‑19, pneumococcal) with proactive outreach  
6. Enhanced primary‑care access / same‑day assessment to divert A&E  
7. Frailty identification and proactive geriatric care for older people  
8. Integrated care system (ICS) data‑sharing platforms for risk stratification  
9. Hospital‑at‑home / early supported discharge for elderly acute cases  
10. Mental‑health crisis alternatives to A&E  
11. Environmental sustainability actions (e.g., low‑carbon inhalers, waste reduction)  
12. Healthcare‑worker (HCW) safety and wellbeing to maintain winter capacity  
13. Supply‑chain resilience for medicines and devices in winter  
14. Digital‑inclusion programmes to equitable access to tech‑enabled care  
15. Accelerated diagnosis pathways for cancer and other long‑term conditions  

